    "diagnosis": "Spindle cell oncocytoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Tumour cells generally show more oval nuclei than do those in schwannoma (which usually contain tapering nuclei with pointed ends). Note the absence of nuclear pseudoinclusions, as can be seen in some meningiomas. Note also the uniformity of nuclear features and absence of mitotic activity.",
